      "structuredContent": {
        "url": "https://github.com/c933103/openrailwaystyle/pull/442",
        "number": 442,
        "state": "open",
        "merged": false,
        "mergeable": true,
        "draft": false,
        "body": "## Cause\nPost-merge site run [43169516681](https://github.com/c933103/openrailwaystyle/actions/runs/43169516681), validation job 131025574439, failed while preparing a staged-provider-pause fixture: recursive scripts copying tried to copy a disappearing Python __pycache__ temporary. Other parallel tests import those Python modules and atomically rename bytecode files. The malformed-calendar assertion and lifecycle acquisition were not the cause.\n\n## Fix\n- Use one source-copy filter at all seven whole source-tree copy sites across six test files. Exclude __pycache__ before recursion, not real source inputs.\n- Keep generated-data copies unchanged; no production behavior, source/provider configuration, retry, test selection, or CI gating changes.\n- Add deterministic coverage showing the old disappearing-bytecode ENOENT, safe filtered copying, nested-cache exclusion and exact preservation of real source, and continued failure for missing real source.\n\n## Validation\n- Regression before the filter: two failures and one pass, including deterministic ENOENT.\n- Focused seven suites: 218 pass, one existing skip, zero failures.\n- npm run build passed; styles/world.style.json unchanged.\n- Two consecutive full npm test runs: 4,114 pass, 13 existing conditional skips, zero failures each (Node 24.22.1; 100.8s and 100.4s).\n- git diff --check passed.\n\nNo provider requests or acquisition dispatches were performed. Fresh exact-head Codex reviews and required CI remain merge gates. This repairs the underlying fixture race rather than blindly rerunning failed production validation.",
        "title": "Exclude transient Python caches from source-copy fixtures",
        "base": "main",
        "base_sha": "25aab4995b21ddc6d2dadcb21ba242639b03e147",
        "head": "fix/fixture-python-cache-race-20261112",
